<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teriitaria II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1790–1858</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Teriitaria II (c. 1790–1858) was queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huahine">Huahine</a> in the Society Islands from 1815 and a wife of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomare-ii">Pōmare II</a> of Tahiti. She supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london-missionary-society">London Missionary Society</a> and led Huahine in resisting French claims during the Franco-Tahitian War of the 1840s. She was deposed by Huahine's chiefs in 1852.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/teriitaria-ii.jpg" alt="Teriitaria II" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antoine Chazal / Ambroise Tardieu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Painting_of_Teriitaria_Ariipaea.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
